I set the left‑action row to weight position negatively (‑1.0) and velocity negatively (‑2.0) so that when the car is on the left side (pos < 0) or moving left (vel < 0) the left score rises. The right‑action row uses positive weights (1.0 for position, 2.0 for velocity) to favor right acceleration when the car is on the right side or moving right. The idle row is zeroed out and I give it a small negative bias (‑0.5) to discourage the controller from defaulting to the idle action, encouraging decisive left/right pushes based on the linear combination of position and velocity. This follows the classic “push left on negative velocity/position, push right on positive” rule and explores with step size 1.0.
