**Explanation**  
I kept the left‑action (action 0) velocity weight at –3.5 so that a negative velocity (moving left) strongly favors the left push, while the right‑action (action 2) keeps a high positive velocity weight (6.0) to accelerate aggressively when the car is moving right.  
I introduced a modest positive position weight (0.3) for the right push to bias action 2 slightly toward positive positions without overriding the velocity signal.  
Both left and right actions retain the –0.5 bias to keep their baseline scores comparable, and the idle action (action 1) stays strongly penalised (bias ≈ –3.6) to avoid accidental selection.  

These adjustments explore a stronger right‑velocity influence and a slightly higher position sensitivity, which should improve the timing of the right‑pushes and potentially reduce the episode length.
